<!--ID=B7267351-473F-409D-9765-754A8EBCDE05;Version=1|{"VoiceNameToIdMapItems":[{"Id":"f1b99834-fbfc-4d32-846d-c4dbd3050c19","Name":"Microsoft Server Speech Text to Speech Voice (en-GB, OllieMultilingualNeural)","ShortName":"en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural","Locale":"en-GB","VoiceType":"StandardVoice"}]}-->
<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-13.50%" pitch="-3.60%">
            The waters are behind you.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            Whatever you passed through to get here — the hard season, the long week, the moment you were not sure you would make it — you are on the other side of it now. You are here. You made it. And He was with you in all of it.
            <break time="9000ms"/>
            The fire did not burn.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            What tried to consume you did not succeed. What threatened to take everything did not take everything. You are here. Breathing. Still held. The flame did not have the final word.
            <break time="9000ms"/>
            He is with you.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            Right now. In this room. In this quiet. He is not far. He has not moved. He is closer than the fear, closer than the thought that says you are alone. He is here.
            <break time="9000ms"/>
            You are called by name.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            Not forgotten. Not misplaced. Known. Your name is in His mouth. He speaks it with care. You are His, and He is yours.
            <break time="9000ms"/>
            You can lay down every fear.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            Not because the fears are not real. But because the one who holds you is more real. More present. More powerful. You do not have to carry them into sleep. You can set them down right here, and He will watch over them and over you.
            <break time="9000ms"/>
            You can rest.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            Let your eyes close. Let your breathing deepen. Let the weight release from your shoulders, your chest, your hands.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            God is with you.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            Fear not.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            Rest now.
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
